.TH SUSPEND 1.SH NAMEsuspend \- remove a process by name.SH SYNOPSIS\fBsuspend\fR[\-s] name.SH DESCRIPTIONDespite its name,\fBsuspend\fRremoves the process running the program\fIname\fRfrom the system; its own usage line says so.  With no such process itrings the bell and answers\fBSorry ! No process found with corressponding name !\fRBy F. R. Schmitt, 1989..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-s\fRalso remove system programs..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOkill, procs